# What evidence a change must produce before finishup will land it.
#
# fast-path      a change touching only these needs no full CI suite
# standard-check must be present and SUCCESS on the PR head for everything else
#
# Fast is earned by the diff, never requested: one path outside this list and
# the whole PR is standard.
#

fast-path      docs/**
fast-path      *.md

# PRs that are not drafts land on green through ci-autoland (~/Automation).
autoland
# CI runs on hosted runners on every push; the PR pipeline reviews every ready PR
# (docs/PR_PIPELINE.md in ~/Automation): nothing merges without the reviewer App.
ci hosted
review bkd-pr-reviewer

standard-check Lint & typecheck
standard-check Unit & integration (Vitest + jest-expo)
standard-check Cross-service e2e
standard-check Agent config drift

# The release flow (~/Automation docs/RELEASES.md): `app-release promote` tags
# master at this version and fast-forwards `prod`, which deploys through
# scripts/ci/deploy.
version        package.json
release        deploy

# files only a workflow writes, straight to the default branch after a merge;
# a commit touching nothing else is not what "behind" or "green" is measured against
generated      docs/implementations.md

# Hosted by exception (~/Automation ADR 0009): the claude-code-action workflows and the
# auto-labeller run Claude Code under the runner's $HOME, which on this machine is David's,
# so they stay on GitHub's image. Optional: a hosted failure (billing, the action) never holds a PR.
optional-check claude-review
optional-check checklist-review
optional-check doc-sync
optional-check label
